WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.001 --> 00:00:03.136
We have major breaking news into CNN.

00:00:03.136 --> 00:00:03.503
Actor

00:00:03.503 --> 00:00:05.372
Alec Baldwin has just been indicted

00:00:05.372 --> 00:00:07.540
by a New Mexico grand jury on charges

00:00:07.540 --> 00:00:09.843
connected to that fatal 2021

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.945
shooting on the set of the film Russe.

00:00:12.212 --> 00:00:13.279
CNN's Josh Campbell

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:13.747
joining us

00:00:13.747 --> 00:00:15.782
now on this, along with legal

00:00:15.782 --> 00:00:17.550
analyst Areva Martin.

00:00:17.550 --> 00:00:18.585
Josh, first to you.

00:00:18.585 --> 00:00:20.720
Tell us what we know here. Yeah.

00:00:20.754 --> 00:00:21.488
So once again,

00:00:21.488 --> 00:00:23.156
Alec Baldwin now criminally

00:00:23.156 --> 00:00:24.624
charged once again.

00:00:24.624 --> 00:00:25.091
Obviously,

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:26.292
we had been reporting earlier

00:00:26.292 --> 00:00:27.394
on after

00:00:27.394 --> 00:00:27.961
that fatal

00:00:27.961 --> 00:00:29.429
shooting in 20, 21

00:00:29.429 --> 00:00:30.463
that the actor had been

00:00:30.463 --> 00:00:31.297
criminally charged.

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:33.466
Those charges were then dropped.

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:34.768
Prosecutors at the time

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:35.535
said that

00:00:35.535 --> 00:00:36.603
that was because new

00:00:36.603 --> 00:00:38.605
evidence came to light in the case

00:00:38.605 --> 00:00:40.006
causing questions

00:00:40.006 --> 00:00:41.341
about a piece of evidence.

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.642
A law enforcement

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:44.144
source at the time told me

00:00:44.144 --> 00:00:45.979
that that was because they learned

00:00:45.979 --> 00:00:46.679
that the weapon

00:00:46.679 --> 00:00:47.280
that was used in

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.082
the shooting had been modified

00:00:49.082 --> 00:00:50.483
in some form.

00:00:50.483 --> 00:00:51.051
And so again,

00:00:51.051 --> 00:00:52.685
those charges had been dropped.

00:00:52.685 --> 00:00:53.820
Prosecutors at the time

00:00:53.820 --> 00:00:54.287
said, though,

00:00:54.287 --> 00:00:56.523
that if they gather new information

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.024
that determine culpability

00:00:58.024 --> 00:00:59.459
on the part of ALEC Baldwin,

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:01.594
they would then possibly refile charges.

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:02.529
We're learning today

00:01:02.529 --> 00:01:03.963
that did indeed happen.

00:01:03.963 --> 00:01:06.066
A grand jury in the state of New Mexico

00:01:06.066 --> 00:01:08.101
returning this two count indictment.

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:08.501
I'll read you

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:10.103
the two charges specifically.

00:01:10.103 --> 00:01:10.870
Count one

00:01:10.870 --> 00:01:13.006
is for involuntary manslaughter,

00:01:13.173 --> 00:01:15.842
negligent use of a firearm, count

00:01:15.842 --> 00:01:17.544
to involuntary manslaughter

00:01:17.544 --> 00:01:20.313
without due caution or circumspection.

00:01:20.313 --> 00:01:22.015
Now, the original prosecutor in the tape

00:01:22.015 --> 00:01:23.283
and the case told me that

00:01:23.283 --> 00:01:24.284
as part of this lengthy

00:01:24.284 --> 00:01:25.618
investigation, authorities

00:01:25.618 --> 00:01:26.252
have determined

00:01:26.252 --> 00:01:27.153
that there was this

00:01:27.153 --> 00:01:29.122
culture of unsafe practices

00:01:29.122 --> 00:01:29.989
on the set

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:30.890
of that movie

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:31.424
with past

00:01:31.424 --> 00:01:33.893
reports of accidental discharges.

00:01:33.993 --> 00:01:34.394
It's worth

00:01:34.394 --> 00:01:36.029
pointing out that actor Alec Baldwin

00:01:36.029 --> 00:01:37.430
all along has indicated

00:01:37.430 --> 00:01:39.065
that he did not pull the trigger

00:01:39.065 --> 00:01:39.966
on that weapon.

00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:41.701
He has maintained his innocence.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:42.902
We just got a statement in here

00:01:42.902 --> 00:01:44.671
to CNN, a very short statement

00:01:44.671 --> 00:01:46.106
from Baldwin's attorney

00:01:46.106 --> 00:01:46.906
saying that

00:01:46.906 --> 00:01:48.942
they look forward to their day in court.

00:01:49.142 --> 00:01:49.542
But again,

00:01:49.542 --> 00:01:51.544
the breaking news now, actor Alec Baldwin

00:01:51.544 --> 00:01:52.078
once again

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.880
now criminally charged in the fatal

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:55.215
shooting on the set of the movie

00:01:55.215 --> 00:01:57.083
Rust in 2021,

00:01:57.083 --> 00:01:58.485
which killed cinematographer

00:01:58.485 --> 00:01:59.319
Helena Hutchins.

00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:04.190
And Areva, how are you reacting to this?

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.993
Well, these are stunning turns of events

00:02:06.993 --> 00:02:08.027
because Brianna,

00:02:08.027 --> 00:02:09.395
we know that Alec Baldwin

00:02:09.395 --> 00:02:10.663
probably thought that this case

00:02:10.663 --> 00:02:12.031
was completely done once

00:02:12.031 --> 00:02:13.867
the other prosecutors

00:02:13.867 --> 00:02:15.535
who were assigned to the case

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.370
dropped the charges against him.

00:02:17.370 --> 00:02:18.805
We know that he's gone public

00:02:18.805 --> 00:02:20.039
talking about the case.

00:02:20.039 --> 00:02:22.175
He has maintained his innocence.

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:24.277
So now to be charged

00:02:24.277 --> 00:02:26.513
with some of the same evidence

00:02:26.513 --> 00:02:28.581
and the same gun, the same issue

00:02:28.581 --> 00:02:30.517
that the prior prosecutors

00:02:30.517 --> 00:02:31.351
had with respect

00:02:31.351 --> 00:02:33.153
to the gun, its issue

00:02:33.153 --> 00:02:35.221
having been mishandled or somehow

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:35.922
damaged by

00:02:35.922 --> 00:02:37.724
the FBI is going to be interesting

00:02:37.724 --> 00:02:40.293
to see how this new team of prosecutors

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:43.463
are able to establish the evidence

00:02:43.463 --> 00:02:44.430
that will be necessary

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:45.798
to get a conviction in this case,

00:02:45.798 --> 00:02:47.767
because you still have this gun

00:02:47.767 --> 00:02:50.303
that was somehow mishandled by the FBI,

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:52.038
which is a central piece of evidence.

00:02:53.106 --> 00:02:55.074
The interesting part about this

00:02:55.074 --> 00:02:55.875
to me, Areva,

00:02:55.875 --> 00:02:56.509
is that

00:02:56.509 --> 00:02:57.977
officials have not been able

00:02:57.977 --> 00:02:58.545
to determine

00:02:58.545 --> 00:03:02.081
how the live ammunition found its way

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:03.750
into that 45

00:03:03.750 --> 00:03:05.051
caliber revolver

00:03:05.051 --> 00:03:06.419
that it was manufactured

00:03:06.419 --> 00:03:07.887
by this Italian company

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:08.821
that specializes

00:03:08.821 --> 00:03:09.189
in the

00:03:09.189 --> 00:03:10.590
kind of reproductions

00:03:10.590 --> 00:03:12.692
that are used on on films like Rust.

00:03:13.059 --> 00:03:13.860
How does that

00:03:13.860 --> 00:03:15.662
potentially complicate the process

00:03:15.662 --> 00:03:17.630
of proving in court

00:03:17.630 --> 00:03:19.299
that Baldwin is guilty

00:03:19.299 --> 00:03:19.866
of two counts

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:22.302
of involuntary manslaughter?

00:03:22.302 --> 00:03:23.870
It's going to be challenging, Boris,

00:03:23.870 --> 00:03:25.171
because the prosecutors

00:03:25.171 --> 00:03:27.774
will have to prove willful disregard.

00:03:28.007 --> 00:03:29.075
And you are right.

00:03:29.075 --> 00:03:30.643
Not only have

00:03:30.643 --> 00:03:32.345
the investigators of prosecutors

00:03:32.345 --> 00:03:34.447
not been able to determine

00:03:34.447 --> 00:03:36.983
how nine bullets or live ammunition

00:03:37.750 --> 00:03:39.152
ended up in the gun.

00:03:39.152 --> 00:03:39.786
They don't even know

00:03:39.786 --> 00:03:42.555
how live ammunition ended up on the set.

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:45.124
That's still a very unanswered question.

00:03:45.158 --> 00:03:46.259
They have not been able to,

00:03:46.259 --> 00:03:47.493
even though the armorer,

00:03:47.493 --> 00:03:48.861
who has also been charged,

00:03:48.861 --> 00:03:49.896
she set to go to trial

00:03:49.896 --> 00:03:51.698
starting in February.

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:53.700
Apparently, she has not provided

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:55.868
any information to law enforcement

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.870
about how that live ammunition

00:03:58.304 --> 00:03:59.639
arrived on this set.

00:03:59.639 --> 00:04:02.208
We know that people should not be killed

00:04:02.342 --> 00:04:04.010
in the making of a movie.

00:04:04.010 --> 00:04:05.111
This was a tragedy

00:04:05.111 --> 00:04:07.046
that should have never happened.

00:04:07.046 --> 00:04:08.348
Two people have been charged.

00:04:08.348 --> 00:04:10.483
And now with Alec Baldwin, a third person

00:04:10.717 --> 00:04:11.584
being charged.

00:04:11.584 --> 00:04:13.620
Clearly, someone is responsible

00:04:13.620 --> 00:04:15.588
for the death of Miss Hutchins.

00:04:15.588 --> 00:04:17.123
But the investigation

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:19.559
seems to have been so shoddy

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.294
that it's not clear to me

00:04:21.294 --> 00:04:22.862
that anyone will be held

00:04:22.862 --> 00:04:24.864
criminally responsible Yeah.

00:04:24.864 --> 00:04:26.733
Josh, how much can that endanger things

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:27.967
when you have

00:04:27.967 --> 00:04:28.801
at least

00:04:28.801 --> 00:04:31.237
in this kind of legal accounting here,

00:04:31.437 --> 00:04:34.440
so many people held accountable

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:36.242
And it's really unclear

00:04:36.242 --> 00:04:38.177
which one should be.

00:04:38.177 --> 00:04:39.212
No, it's a great question.

00:04:39.212 --> 00:04:39.379
You know,

00:04:39.379 --> 00:04:41.214
I posed this to prosecutors early on

00:04:41.214 --> 00:04:41.814
and they said that

00:04:41.814 --> 00:04:43.549
they will conduct this investigation

00:04:43.549 --> 00:04:44.350
and hold accountable

00:04:44.350 --> 00:04:46.986
anyone that they believe was responsible.

00:04:46.986 --> 00:04:47.854
But it's worth pointing out,

00:04:47.854 --> 00:04:49.922
after those initial charges came out,

00:04:49.922 --> 00:04:51.557
we heard from numerous

00:04:51.557 --> 00:04:53.293
legal experts who were quite stunned,

00:04:53.293 --> 00:04:54.460
actually saying that you know,

00:04:54.460 --> 00:04:55.862
we can understand charging

00:04:55.862 --> 00:04:57.430
someone who

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.232
was responsible for a live round

00:04:59.232 --> 00:05:00.433
being in that gun.

00:05:00.433 --> 00:05:01.634
But there's just been this question

00:05:01.634 --> 00:05:02.635
about an actor,

00:05:02.635 --> 00:05:05.972
someone who was told on set allegedly

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:08.007
by one of the prop

00:05:08.007 --> 00:05:10.443
masters that this weapon was, quote,

00:05:10.443 --> 00:05:12.111
cold, that it did not have

00:05:12.111 --> 00:05:13.613
any type of ammunition in it.

00:05:13.613 --> 00:05:14.047
That person

00:05:14.047 --> 00:05:15.882
then handed it to Alec Baldwin.

00:05:15.882 --> 00:05:16.749
And so this is going to be,

00:05:16.749 --> 00:05:18.584
I think, a central part of

00:05:18.584 --> 00:05:19.819
Alec Baldwin's defense.

00:05:19.819 --> 00:05:20.353
Two parts.

00:05:20.353 --> 00:05:21.120
First, you know,

00:05:21.120 --> 00:05:22.955
should an actor be responsible

00:05:22.955 --> 00:05:25.291
for then checking the gun

00:05:25.291 --> 00:05:26.959
and then no knowing the difference

00:05:26.959 --> 00:05:28.628
between a live round of ammunition

00:05:28.628 --> 00:05:30.063
and a so-called dummy round.

00:05:30.063 --> 00:05:31.264
We know that there was a live round

00:05:31.264 --> 00:05:32.899
of ammunition in there, ultimately.

00:05:32.899 --> 00:05:33.800
There's also the question

00:05:33.800 --> 00:05:35.835
about the integrity of the gun itself

00:05:35.835 --> 00:05:36.502
as the reviews,

00:05:36.502 --> 00:05:37.904
which I was just talking about.

00:05:37.904 --> 00:05:39.505
Whenever the FBI was brought in

00:05:39.505 --> 00:05:39.972
to conduct

00:05:39.972 --> 00:05:41.374
an analysis of this gun,

00:05:41.374 --> 00:05:44.210
they did multiple tests on the weapon.

00:05:44.310 --> 00:05:45.945
The central question there was,

00:05:45.945 --> 00:05:47.814
could this gun go off

00:05:47.814 --> 00:05:50.083
if Alec Baldwin did not pull the trigger?

00:05:50.083 --> 00:05:51.351
Of course, he has claimed all along

00:05:51.351 --> 00:05:52.919
that he did not pull the trigger.

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:54.053
What the FBI determined

00:05:54.053 --> 00:05:55.121
through their testing is

00:05:55.121 --> 00:05:55.855
that gun

00:05:55.855 --> 00:05:57.423
could not have fired

00:05:57.423 --> 00:05:59.192
unless someone actually pulled

00:05:59.192 --> 00:05:59.859
the trigger.

00:05:59.859 --> 00:06:01.160
Now, as Areva mentioned,

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:02.962
the gun did get destroyed

00:06:02.962 --> 00:06:04.731
during the course of that testing.

00:06:04.731 --> 00:06:06.632
I read through this lengthy report

00:06:06.632 --> 00:06:08.634
from the FBI analysts in Quantico.

00:06:08.634 --> 00:06:09.469
What they indicated

00:06:09.469 --> 00:06:11.471
was we're talking about an older gun

00:06:11.471 --> 00:06:12.338
this isn't a prop gun.

00:06:12.338 --> 00:06:14.407
This was an actual functioning weapon

00:06:14.807 --> 00:06:15.808
that through the course

00:06:15.808 --> 00:06:16.743
of multiple rounds

00:06:16.743 --> 00:06:17.543
of testing

00:06:17.543 --> 00:06:18.745
the gun pieces

00:06:18.745 --> 00:06:20.747
inside the gun ultimately failed

00:06:21.114 --> 00:06:22.281
causing destruction.

00:06:22.281 --> 00:06:22.615
And that's

00:06:22.615 --> 00:06:23.750
what Alec Baldwin's team

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:25.418
seized on, saying, look, the gun itself,

00:06:25.418 --> 00:06:26.986
there were problems with it.

00:06:26.986 --> 00:06:27.420
But, you know,

00:06:27.420 --> 00:06:29.122
I went back to law enforcement,

00:06:29.122 --> 00:06:31.124
to the prosecutors asking

00:06:31.124 --> 00:06:32.425
They indicated that no, at the time

00:06:32.425 --> 00:06:34.227
that the weapon was used on

00:06:34.227 --> 00:06:35.027
that said

00:06:35.027 --> 00:06:35.928
analysts believe

00:06:35.928 --> 00:06:37.196
that it could not have been fired

00:06:37.196 --> 00:06:38.097
without someone actually

00:06:38.097 --> 00:06:39.065
pulling the trigger,

00:06:39.065 --> 00:06:40.199
which I think finally is

00:06:40.199 --> 00:06:42.068
why as you look at these charges,

00:06:42.068 --> 00:06:44.103
this all seems to center around

00:06:44.103 --> 00:06:44.937
negligence.

00:06:44.937 --> 00:06:46.205
I mean, it's right in count one,

00:06:46.205 --> 00:06:48.241
negligent use of a firearm.

00:06:48.241 --> 00:06:49.175
If you are someone

00:06:49.175 --> 00:06:50.109
who is in possession

00:06:50.109 --> 00:06:51.878
of a functioning firearm

00:06:51.878 --> 00:06:53.780
and you pointed at someone

00:06:53.780 --> 00:06:55.348
and you manipulate that weapon,

00:06:55.348 --> 00:06:56.315
whether that's the trigger

00:06:56.315 --> 00:06:57.917
or the hammer on the gun

00:06:57.917 --> 00:06:59.886
and it goes off and someone dies,

00:06:59.886 --> 00:07:01.254
are you responsible

00:07:01.254 --> 00:07:02.121
prosecutors here

00:07:02.121 --> 00:07:03.489
saying ultimately, yes,

00:07:03.489 --> 00:07:05.558
or I should say a grand jury coming

00:07:05.558 --> 00:07:06.726
now and saying, yes,

00:07:06.726 --> 00:07:08.327
that Alec Baldwin should be indicted

00:07:08.327 --> 00:07:09.662
on those criminal charges?

00:07:09.662 --> 00:07:10.263
Of course, we'll wait

00:07:10.263 --> 00:07:11.164
and see what happens

00:07:11.164 --> 00:07:12.632
next in the prosecution.

00:07:12.632 --> 00:07:14.200
There was always this question about,

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:15.568
you know, early on

00:07:15.568 --> 00:07:16.402
whether Alec Baldwin

00:07:16.402 --> 00:07:17.503
would plead to anything.

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:18.538
His team was adamant

00:07:18.538 --> 00:07:19.138
that he wasn't

00:07:19.138 --> 00:07:20.139
playing to anything

00:07:20.139 --> 00:07:21.974
that he determined or believed

00:07:21.974 --> 00:07:23.876
that he was innocent of these charges.

00:07:23.876 --> 00:07:24.177
And again,

00:07:24.177 --> 00:07:24.577
that statement

00:07:24.577 --> 00:07:25.711
we just got from his attorney

00:07:25.711 --> 00:07:26.679
say that they look forward

00:07:26.679 --> 00:07:28.314
to having their day in court.

00:07:28.314 --> 00:07:29.015
And then the final point

00:07:29.015 --> 00:07:30.116
I'll mention is Areva

00:07:30.116 --> 00:07:31.384
centered on which this is so important

00:07:31.384 --> 00:07:32.051
is that we're not talking

00:07:32.051 --> 00:07:34.120
about a separate group of prosecutors

00:07:34.120 --> 00:07:35.855
from the original team

00:07:35.855 --> 00:07:37.023
that filed charges.

00:07:37.023 --> 00:07:37.657
This prosecution

00:07:37.657 --> 00:07:39.325
has had all kinds of issues.

00:07:39.325 --> 00:07:39.959
At one point,

00:07:39.959 --> 00:07:40.860
there was one person

00:07:40.860 --> 00:07:42.295
who was brought on to the prosecution

00:07:42.295 --> 00:07:42.862
team.

00:07:42.862 --> 00:07:43.729
It turned out

00:07:43.729 --> 00:07:45.865
she was a Republican legislature

00:07:45.865 --> 00:07:47.400
in New Mexico,

00:07:47.400 --> 00:07:48.434
a legislator in New Mexico

00:07:48.434 --> 00:07:49.969
who is also working on the case.

00:07:49.969 --> 00:07:51.304
The Baldwin team cried foul.

00:07:51.304 --> 00:07:52.205
They're saying, look, this

00:07:52.205 --> 00:07:53.473
probably smacks of politics.

00:07:53.473 --> 00:07:55.274
And so bottom line, a new special

00:07:55.274 --> 00:07:56.943
prosecution team was brought in.

00:07:56.943 --> 00:07:59.111
That's the team that ultimately presented

00:07:59.111 --> 00:08:00.246
this to the grand jury.

00:08:00.246 --> 00:08:00.780
The grand jury

00:08:00.780 --> 00:08:01.414
finding that, yes,

00:08:01.414 --> 00:08:01.948
Alec Baldwin

00:08:01.948 --> 00:08:04.650
should be indicted on two counts.

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:07.487
All right, Josh and Areva, so it goes on.

00:08:07.753 --> 00:08:08.754
We'll continue to follow

00:08:08.754 --> 00:08:09.655
it along with you.

